    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d606">

                <pb facs="0503" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.512/165</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 774</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-19">May 19,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received June 5.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Legation’s despatches no. 640 of February 24, 1942 and no. 658 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">656</hi>] of March 3, 1942, and to report that, in
                    accordance with the authorization contained in the Department’s telegram no. 84
                    of March [<hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>] 4, 1942, 11 p.m., an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi><anchor n="62" xml:id="d606-f1"/> was
                    left with my Spanish colleague, copies of which are enclosed, on the subject of
                    the payment by American citizens to the Customs of the so-called Auxiliary
                    Social Relief Tax.</p>
                <p>When I presented the <hi rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi> to my Spanish
                    colleague, he expressed great satisfaction with its conciliatory character.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rives Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d606-f1" n="62" xml:id="d606-f1-content">
                <p>See draft of <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>, <ref target="#pg490">p.
                        490</ref>.</p>
            </note>
